<http://data.silknow.org/object/9d8cab37-6582-3303-bc5d-74b88ca9d50c/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Complete wall panel woven after designer produced for the Cabinet des Parades for the Palais du Pardo outside of Madrid. Cream-colored satin ground brocaded and embroidered with polychrome silks. Design, top to bottom: three butterflies within a square formed of fliage and pink blossoms; rose sprigs and festoon; parrot (embroidered); blue vase holding asters; pair of affronted pheasants; bird-cage (embroidered); ribbon festoons and blue cornflower sprigs; a golden mask with red-and-gold festoon. Yellow-and-blue striped and white corded selvedges, complete on both sides. Six blue stamps on back. Small breaks in satin near selvedges at center and ends. Few small brown stains."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/9d8cab37-6582-3303-bc5d-74b88ca9d50c> .

<http://data.silknow.org/production/dd0e2f88-786c-37d1-9b2d-e6245b0ac269>
